  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company’s core CBD and THC beverage operations are showing early signs of stabilization and sequential demand recovery, with management citing several months of improving trends and a strong start to the fiscal year. The niche wellness market backdrop appears steady, and no adverse regulatory developments are highlighted. Product-level gross margins remain healthy, reinforcing underlying brand appeal, though the broader sales recovery is still rebuilding from a low base. Trader attention has intensified, viewing the stock as an asymmetric turnaround play amid improving operational momentum.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has pursued a deliberate “reset,” focusing on aggressive balance sheet restructuring and margin discipline to stem losses and shore up liquidity. Key strategic actions include the acquisition of Bluebird Botanicals to broaden the customer base and unlock synergies, regaining NYSE listing compliance, and securing flexible credit arrangements. The CEO’s commentary conveys cautious encouragement without overpromising, pointing to consecutive monthly improvements. Market reaction suggests growing, albeit tentative, confidence in execution, reflected in surging volume and sharp price moves as investors reassess the turnaround story.",
